-- Verdict **PASS** iff `expected_gain ≥ 2 × total_cost` (and net > 0), else **COST_GATE_SKIP**. Every number is logged in the `cost_gate` block (inputs, costs, expected gain, ratio, method, verdict, assumptions). Pack blocks are `stage=preliminary` (non-binding); `final_gate_from_prepare` / execute_pass produce the binding `stage=final` block.
-- `do_not_place=True` keeps meaning “this script never places”; `auto_place_eligible` is the separate FULL AUTO eligibility flag.
+   Fail-closed checks: US regular session (NYSE hours + 2026–27 holidays); run-QA verdict `skill=classic-rsi-1h-run-qa`, `checked_at` ≤ 60 min, run_id match; order-QA `skill=classic-real-money-order-qa-gate`, ≤ 15 min, different file, `pack_sha256` equal to the sha this run prints; live quote ≤ 60 s, bid < ask; live cash ≤ 60 s, book asOf ≤ 15 min; `cash − units×ask − open_fee ≥ 2500` (getCost open fee required; units auto-shrink); name 30%/15% and sleeve 45% caps on market value **and** cost basis; min $400; drift ≤ 0.5×ATR(1H); final cost gate PASS (risk-exit sells: RISK_EXIT); 0 < SL < bid; idempotency lock `audit/placed/<sha(pack_id)>.lock` and no same-instrument position opened after the signal. Exit 0 = GO, 2 = NO-GO. Without order-QA → `NO-GO / ORDER_QA_PENDING` + `ready_for_order_qa=true` + `pack_sha256`.
+5. QA Bot (**classic-real-money-order-qa-gate**) reviews the execute_pass audit and writes a verdict with `skill`, `checked_at`, `pack_id`/`symbol`, `run_id` and the `pack_sha256`; re-run execute_pass with the **same** inputs (quote still ≤ 60 s) → **GO**. If the quote expired or size changed, the sha changes → new order-QA.
+6. On GO, Trader_Classic copies `order_payloads` **verbatim** to the MCP (`user-OfersClaw5`): buys `{instrumentId, isBuy:true, leverage:1, units, stopLossRate, takeProfitRate}`, sells `{positionId, instrumentId, isBuy:false, unitsToDeduct}` — sells first, re-reading cash between sequenced places. No chat authorization under FULL AUTO. RISK_OFF notes never become short orders.
+
+### Cost gate (`cost_gate.py`, v2 fix1)
+
+- `total_cost = spread + open_fee (buy legs) + close_fee + overnight + tax_est`, all ≥ 0, total > 0.
+  - spread = `max(spread_usd, (ask − bid) × units)`; final stage needs bid < ask and `quote_ts` ≤ 60 s (optional independent mark within 0.1%).
+  - fees from prepare/getCost — **required at the final stage** (no defaults). Preliminary only: 0.15% spread and $0.75 per order (real Classic fills 2026-10-07 ADBE/GS/CAT $500 each, keys).
+  - `tax_est = 25% × max(realized_pnl, 0)` on every sell leg (Israeli capital-gains rate).
+- Expected gain = directional EV, after tax (`× 0.75` when positive):
+  - RSI: `EV = units × [p(TP − ask) − (1 − p)(ask − SL)]`. `p` needs a cited source. Default = classic_rsi 1H backtest 12/19 = 0.632, **Wilson 95% lower bound 0.410** (in-sample, n=19). Break-even for the 1.5/2.0 ATR bracket is 0.4286, so with the default p every RSI pack is `COST_GATE_SKIP` until better (cited) evidence is supplied via `--p-hit/--p-source`.
+  - Rebalance add / trim / sell / rotation: an `edge` dict is required — `method ∈ {rs_expected_return, trend_expected_return}`, `expected_return_pct`, `horizon_days`, `evidence{source, n}` (rotation also `held_expected_return_pct`). Add: notional × er; trim/sell: −notional × er_held; rotation (one combined gate, `legs[]`): buy_notional × (er_new − er_held). No edge → SKIP. Typed USD gains are not accepted.
+- Verdict **PASS** iff `EV_after_tax ≥ 2 × total_cost` and net > 0; **COST_GATE_SKIP** otherwise; **COST_GATE_INVALID** on bad/missing inputs (negative fees/units, p ∉ (0,1), bid ≥ ask, stale/missing quote, assumed inputs at final, total ≤ 0); **RISK_EXIT** for listed hard risk exits (numbers still recorded).
+- `do_not_place=True` keeps meaning “this script never places”; `auto_place_eligible` requires a preliminary PASS, and a `--force` auto run is never eligible.
 
